-- title:
--   Representability of endomorphism-stable Hopf ideals with rank-k quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $A$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf $R$-algebra structure and finitely generated as an $R$-module, let $\iota$ be an index type, let $\sigma : \iota \to (A \to_{\mathrm{alg}[R]} A)$ be a family of $R$-algebra endomorphisms of $A$, and let $k$ be a natural number. The assertion is that there exist a scheme $H$, a morphism $p : H \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, and, for every commutative $R$-algebra $B$, a bijection `pt` between (i) the set of points $N$ of `Module.Grassmannian B (B ⊗[R] A) k`, that is $B$-submodules $N$ of $B \otimes_R A$ with projective quotient of rank $k$, subject to three conditions: $N$ is closed under multiplication by arbitrary elements of $B \otimes_R A$; the ideal generated by $N$ satisfies [`Ideal.IsHopfIdeal' B`](def/HopfAlgebra_HopfIdealQuotient.html#L79), i.e. every $x$ in it has $\mathrm{comul}(x)$ killed by the map $(B\otimes_R A)\otimes_B(B\otimes_R A) \to Q \otimes_B Q$ induced by the quotient maps onto $Q$ by that ideal, has $\mathrm{counit}(x) = 0$, and has antipode again in the ideal; and $N$ is stable under the $B$-base change of the $R$-linear map underlying each $\sigma_i$; and (ii) the set of morphisms $g : \operatorname{Spec} B \to H$ with $g$ followed by $p$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to B$. Furthermore there exists a witness `hmap` that for every $R$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ the submodule `Module.Grassmannian.map φ N` again satisfies the three conditions over $B'$, such that `pt` is natural: $(\mathrm{pt}_{B'}(\varphi_*N))$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi)$ followed by $\mathrm{pt}_B(N)$; and there exist $m$ and a closed immersion $\iota_P : H \to \operatorname{Proj}$ of the homogeneous-polynomial algebra in $m+1$ variables over $R$ with $\iota_P$ followed by `ProjSpace.π R m` equal to $p$.
--
--   This is the representability, by a projective $R$-scheme, of the functor of finite locally free closed subgroup schemes of corank $k$ of the finite group scheme $\operatorname{Spec} A$ that are stable under a prescribed family of endomorphisms; it refines the Hilbert-scheme-type statement [`Module.Grassmannian.exists_scheme_represents_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace`](thm.html#Module.Grassmannian.exists_scheme_represents_and_isClosedImmersion_toProjSpace) by cutting out a closed subfunctor. It is used in the construction of the moduli schemes attached to formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
-- source:
